WEBVTT

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.910
I opened my eyes and saw the front door.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.910
Shit!

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.920
I was supposed to sit in on the
planning meeting first thing in the morning!

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.530
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.530
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:00:54.950 --> 00:01:00.080
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:00:54.950 --> 00:01:00.080
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.710
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.710
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.500
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.500
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.510
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.510
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.340
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.340
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:23.730
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:23.730
If I reach out my hand

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.100
hajimete no kimochi

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.100
Will you understand my feelings?

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.480
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.480
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.860
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.860
I love you more and more every second

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.990
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.990
We're still far from a happy ending

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:49.960
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:49.960
But I want to make it come true

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.420
tsuzuite yuku

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.420
Our story continues

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.650
I'm gonna be late!

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.680
Crap, I'm cutting it close!

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.730
I ended up wearing the same clothes I wore yesterday.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.190
My only sustenance is energy drinks,

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:17.280
and convenience store boxed lunches.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.550
I don't want to live...

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:23.950
...like this anymore.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:29.950
It's been like this ever since I
started working in manga publishing.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.210
You're late, Onodera!

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.720
I'm very sorry!

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.050
I told you to be on time!

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:41.950
You shouldn't be coming in after your bosses!

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.470
I am terribly sorry!

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.980
I guess you can't be bothered if
you're not participating in the meeting.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.850
Sorry!

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.230
Overslept again!

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.060
Man, am I sleepy!

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.620
The older I get, the harder it gets to wake up.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:00.490
Isn't it normally the other way around?

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.910
Takano was saying...

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.190
...I should see how they run a planning meeting,

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:09.500
so we agreed I'd sit in on this one.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.360
This is a meeting...

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.940
...where the managers of each department meet,

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.270
and decide on how many copies of a certain manga to print.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.510
In Marukawa publishing's case,

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.500
this means order processing who manages the inventory,

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.760
the business unit who manages sales,

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.220
the editors who make the book,

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:33.050
and the people with a say.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.530
Then we will now officially start this meeting.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.170
Oh, right.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.050
Sorry,

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.780
but I was kinda busy, so I didn't have
time to go over these documents.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.530
I'll read them now, so just carry on.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.530
Mr. Izaka, again?

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.540
Oh, can it.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.860
A supervisor never has enough time.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:57.010
Then let us begin this meeting without the supervisor.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.300
We on the order processing side...

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:03.180
...would like a first printing of 200,000 copies.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:04.430
That's not enough.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:11.370
If we look at that author's sales, you can
easily start with 240,000 to 250,000 copies.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:13.190
Are you stupid?

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.690
This is the first volume of a new series.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.070
There's no reason to take such a risk.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.480
Lacking vision, like always.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.570
What?!

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.320
We'll start with 300,000 copies.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.320
Go get your coffee, Takano!

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.330
On what basis?!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.330
Stop fucking around!

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.270
You're the ones fucking around!

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.330
Wh-What's going on?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.750
I'm basing this on our survey
results of the work's serialization!

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.960
On the number of copies sold until now!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.650
My intuition!

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.340
Based on that, anything less than 300,000 is unthinkable.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.560
Intuition?

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:46.340
How stupid is that!

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.910
What the hell is that supposed to mean, your "intuition"?

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.360
Why's everyone so antagonistic?

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:55.350
I don't want to hear anything from
people who don't even have intuition!

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.100
What the fuck?!

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:00.860
You haven't forgotten about when you misread
the number of copies we'd need just recently, right?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.820
I haven't forgotten at all!

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.370
I won't take anything less than 300,000 copies.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.120
We'll print 260,000!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.000
There's no way we can think of
printing more than 230,000 copies!

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.000
Then why don't we compromise at
around 270,000 copies, plus a few?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.750
Too wishy-washy!

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:21.800
You're right!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.010
I was thinking the same thing.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.860
Do you have anything to add to this?

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.510
Not really...

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:37.390
But I do think this volume will sell well.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:38.520
What?

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.520
Of course it will sell!

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:46.260
If you all know that, then what are you fighting about?

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.410
Why was just watching that so exhausting?

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:58.250
Am I actually expected to discuss my
own project in there at some point?

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.420
My stomach...

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.180
If it isn't Onodera!

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.120
Mr. Sumi! I haven't heard from you in ages.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.680
What are you up to these days?

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.790
I thought you quit editing.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.690
No, I ended up in the same business.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:28.270
Oh? Then why didn't you tell me you were working
in Marukawa's literature department?

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:30.320
Oh, actually...

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:35.300
Right now I'm editing shojo manga.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.830
Shojo manga?

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.450
But why?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.340
I read you as a man of literature, through and through.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.170
Well...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.090
I guess you could say a lot has happened.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:49.560
Sir...

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:52.090
Yes, of course.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.820
Perhaps you two already know each
other, working in the same company.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:58.600
This is my editor, Mr. Hasegawa.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.120
Onodera here...

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.030
...is the heir to the Onodera Publishing throne!

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.590
Sir, please stop!

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.000
Onodera Publishing?

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.390
But now I'm just a regular employee here at Marukawa.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.730
Mr. Takano.

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:15.480
Huh?

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:16.120
Sir,

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:20.480
this is my boss. The Emerald's editor-in-chief.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:21.870
Masamune Takano.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.540
It's nice to meet you.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.920
My name is Takano.

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:28.780
And this is the writer Ryouichi Sumi.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.520
I was his editor at my previous company.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.290
Shojo manga are nice,

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:39.140
but Onodera here is really more suited to literature.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:42.390
Don't keep him here too long.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.910
Sir, that's...

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:48.150
Your taxi is here, sir.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.350
Then it's time for me to go.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.990
I'm leaving now.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.800
Yes, sir!

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:07.200
I'm sorry for interrupting you in the hallway.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.920
It's not a problem at all.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:13.430
But are you really the heir to
the Onodera Publishing Company?

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.350
Well...

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:17.120
I guess so...

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:22.420
Sorry, but I don't want it to really get around.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:23.940
If you say so.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.240
But why?

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.830
You can take pride in it.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.030
No.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:34.830
I'm glad if my father's company is considered valuable,

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:39.760
but his success has nothing to do with me.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.590
If anything, it's been weighing me down.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:48.110
Which is exactly why I quit that place.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.710
You're quite humble.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.580
Did you come to us because you
were interested in doing manga?

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:01.380
No. I asked to be put into the literature department,

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:02.730
but shojo manga is where I ended up.

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.730
What a disaster!

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.510
I guess...

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.880
Takano's a hard case, huh?

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:26.620
He's wicked good at his job, but he can't
expect everyone to work at his level.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.380
I hear that's what got him in
trouble at his last company, too.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.270
Well, but that...

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.460
But if you do exactly what he says,

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.140
you always get the right results!

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.140
Excuse me.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.560
What the hell?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.400
Why am I defending Takano?

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:49.710
Hey.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:52.400
Are you interested in reading Mr. Sumi's latest book?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.820
Wow.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:02.180
You can really tell this is Mr. Sumi's work.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.840
They really put some money into this.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:12.610
Looks like they used Asian Esperansa
paper for the inside cover,

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:15.250
and made the spine pale indigo.

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.170
What a great setup!

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.210
I knew it! It was designed by Hirano.

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:22.570
Good work.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:29.310
Hard-cover books are real works of art.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.550
I'm not saying what we're doing is worthless, just...

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.450
I guess...

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.600
...I always did like literature.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.440
What the hell was that for?!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.710
If you've got time to daydream, finish your work.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.420
It is finished!

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.460
Then hurry up and start the next thing.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.640
I complete my work in a timely manner,

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:58.090
I don't need to be told to do each task individually!

00:10:58.430 --> 00:10:59.290
What?!

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.590
Here you are! Onodera!

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.350
I brought you all sorts of books.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.600
You can take whichever you like.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:09.100
Really?

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.380
Oh, it looks like I've already got all of these books.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:16.590
I should've known!

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.670
But if you'd let me have them,

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:19.860
I'd like to keep them!

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.300
Hey, want to go get a drink later?

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:25.420
Today?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.340
Sure.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:28.960
You know, just to exchange some information.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.340
Well, I'd have to check my...

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:33.130
Don't bother.

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:34.910
I'm sorry,

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:37.460
but I'd like to ask you to not bother my employees.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:40.760
Someone who can't even do his job right
has no business going out drinking.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.740
You've always been hard on people, Takano.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:46.310
Hard on yourself and hard on others.

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:48.190
I'm really sorry.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:49.200
Don't worry about it.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.020
I'll take a rain check.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:55.140
I'll invite you when the demon editor isn't around.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:59.970
If he gets scary, you can always
come to the literature department.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:05.280
Marukawa's pretty flexible when it comes to transfers.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:08.780
Onodera.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:13.460
I'd like a copy of the data we'll need for our next meeting.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:15.860
Yes, sir!

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:17.800
That's right...

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.870
Ever since I got here, I've been so
focused on getting my work done...

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.550
...that I didn't even think about it.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:26.530
Request for transfer...

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:30.560
That's right, I could always ask to transfer.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:50.140
Thank you!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.730
Dinner's another convenience store meal tonight.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:59.090
I should go to the library and return this book.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:04.010
Who gives people more work
as they're about to leave?!

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:16.860
Why does he think he can just butt in like that?

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.230
It's bad enough if he tells me what to do,

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:22.830
but you don't pick a fight with other employees!

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:46.510
At night, the library in the
housing district is the only quiet spot.

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:50.210
Ah, how good it feels...

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:54.760
Why are you here?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.440
Mr. Takano!

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.690
Why are you following me?

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.450
Why the hell would I be following you?!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:10.310
Has it occurred to you that I
might be returning a book, too?

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:16.560
Do you borrow books from the library often?

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:17.760
Yeah.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:20.080
They've got a lot of out of print and rare books here.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.810
Ones you can't get in a bookstore anymore.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.040
He comes here for the same reason.

00:14:28.710 --> 00:14:30.480
Then I'll be going now.

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:34.600
I don't want you getting chummy
with people from other departments.

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:37.100
And why is that?

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:39.600
It's annoying.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:42.610
It's not like we were talking about things unrelated to work.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.150
You were though.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.610
And how is that your business?!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:53.120
Mr. Hasegawa was just trying to make
me feel welcome, and you had to butt in!

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.860
Or what, are you jealous of Mr. Hasegawa?

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:06.180
That's it, that's why you were picking a fight.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.510
Goodbye.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.770
What the hell?

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.640
That was his cue to deny it and make fun of me!

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:24.400
So why did Takano-?

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:32.410
You idiot!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.910
You could've cracked your head open!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.170
Watch where the hell you're going!

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.410
Th-Thank you.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:42.520
I guess I slipped on some of these fallen leaves.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.170
That was scary...

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.550
U-Um, Takano...

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:05.990
Uh...

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:08.940
You were always in the library back then, too.

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:11.540
Will you please let me go?

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:12.800
You...

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:15.350
You said some strange things.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:19.000
How much do you remember from
what happened ten years ago?

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.170
Uh, Takano...

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.210
I'm sure you haven't forgotten the time...

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:27.840
...you confessed your feelings to me.

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:33.470
What about the time we went home together?

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:39.300
And how you slept at my place then?

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:40.950
Just let me go!

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:41.850
Let me go please!

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:47.100
And how about the fact that I knew who you were,

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.770
even before you confessed to me?

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.110
What the hell are you doing?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.570
Just leave me alone!

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:42.620
Takano...

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:44.520
What did he just say?

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:51.630
That ten years ago, he knew who I was
even before I had confessed to him?

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:05.230
Strictly speaking, it was ten years ago,

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.230
but I don't really remember what happened anymore.

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:14.440
It's not like we were going out for a long time.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:19.300
Then after that, I actively tried to forget what happened.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:27.810
And I have no clue as to what
he's been up to these ten years.

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:37.160
Did that come out of Takano's room?

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.580
Hey!

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:42.100
You stay inside.

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:51.280
Uh, well...

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:53.270
Good evening!

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:54.810
What are you doing here?

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.510
If it's about work,

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:02.920
you can call him or write an email.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.530
No, I live here.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.060
I live next door to him.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:10.460
What, you're stalking him?

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:14.180
It's a mere coincidence!

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:17.800
If I had known he was living next door,

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.840
I would have never moved into this apartment!

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:21.100
It wouldn't be good for me to...

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:24.320
I told you to stay away from Masamune.

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:29.800
Don't lead him on any more, it's a nuisance.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:34.270
I'm the one who's bothered by all of this.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:38.070
Mr. Takano and I have nothing
beyond a working relationship,

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:42.510
I would appreciate if you refrained from claiming...

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:44.740
...that I was the reason he got messed up.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:45.830
Do you...

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.830
...really mean that?

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.330
Why would I joke about such things?

00:19:55.850 --> 00:20:01.290
You've got some nerve, causing such problems
and then conveniently forgetting them all.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:03.800
You've really got some nerve.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.400
I've told you, I didn't do anything to him!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:12.600
Masamune and I have known each other since college.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:21.050
He'd always been a jaded guy
because of family problems,

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:27.050
but then one day, he utterly fell apart.

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:31.170
He started skipping all his classes,

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.030
and began drinking heavily.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:39.130
He became carelessly promiscuous.

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:44.490
He was really far gone.

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:49.260
Why do you think he got that way?

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:52.270
How would I know?

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:57.820
This guy he had gone out with in
high school suddenly kicked him out,

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:01.830
and disappeared without giving
him a chance to find out the reason.

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:03.920
Years pass,

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:06.780
and just when I thought he was finally over it,

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:12.860
some old classmate of that guy found a clue or something.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:20.100
Apparently that guy had a fiancé at
the time he was dating Masamune.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:24.770
So the guy who asked him out was dating two people.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:30.770
How many people around Masamune
do you think fit that profile?

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:34.150
No, it wasn't like that!

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:37.300
That thing with the fiancé is a misunderstanding!

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:42.440
Misunderstanding or not,

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:47.300
nothing will change the fact that you hurt Masamune!

